'''Walpurgisnacht''' (ワルプルギスの夜, ''Warupurugisu no Yoru'', '''Walpurgis Night''') is a [[:Category:Witch Enemies|Witch]] enemy that appears in the [[Puella Magi Madoka Magica Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 5.5 Update|Version 5.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Walpurgisnacht
|image = E 277.png
|appearance = [[Puella Magi Madoka Magica Collaboration Event]]
|money drop = 8,000¢ - 31,600¢
}}

==Enemy==
Walpurgisnacht is the most dangerous enemy from the entire Madoka Magica collab. This is because her Omni Strikes can hit up to 1500 range away from her and slow units somehow surviving it, complete with Base Destroyer and her fast attack rate. Also keep in mind that like all Witch enemies, she is not considered a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy despite aesthetically being in the air.

==Strategy==
Surprisingly, this enemy becomes very easy to beat if you have unlocked both [[Li'l Madoka (Rare Cat)|Li'l Madoka]] and [[Li'l Homura (Special Cat)|Li'l Homura]] and use them in battle. The [[Cat Combo]] called [[My Very Best Friend (Combo)|My Very Best Friend]] involving these Cats will further improve the effect of their Witch Killer ability by a massive factor. You can use also any of the [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] from the collaboration should you have received them; see [[Puella Magi Madoka Magica Collaboration Event/Gacha Drop|here]] for a list of units who have the ability. Of them, [[Homura Akemi (Uber Rare Cat)|Homura]] has the best matchup due to her slow immunity, allowing her to recover immediately if she is ever knocked back. Without [[:Category:Witch Killer Cats|Witch Killers]], the battle becomes more challenging if not outright impossible.

Alternatively, you can use [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] boosted with combos to slowly drain its health, but be aware that in higher magnifications, Stone Cat can be destroyed immediately due to the massive [[Critical Hit|Critical]] damage unless at a high level, and using it alone takes a long time to win. Still, Stone Cat can work wonders with stalling Walpurgisnacht while other units deal damage. Even if you don't have [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]], you can use [[Talents|talented]] [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] and speed combos. Keep in mind this only works with a M speed combo and maybe lvl 8-10 or lvl 10 with a Sm speed combo. You also need Slow Resist to a good level so that it can move forward as soon as the knockback animation finishes.

